{"step_index":353,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T15:48:29Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T12:48:29-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T12:48:32-03:00\nThe search for \"\"LockedIn AI\" interview copilot how it works\" returned the following summary:\nLockedIn AI is an interview assistant designed to provide real-time support during live technical and behavioral interviews. It functions as a digital \"copilot\" by listening to the conversation, analyzing questions, and generating suggested responses or coding solutions on your screen.\n\n### How It Works\n*   **Real-Time Listening & Analysis:** The tool uses speech recognition to transcribe the interview in real-time. It processes the interviewer's questions and provides instant AI-generated guidance, such as coding help, system design suggestions, or behavioral response structures.\n*   **Stealth Features:** A key selling point of LockedIn AI is its \"Stealth Mode,\" which is designed to make the copilot interface invisible to common screen-sharing software and video platforms, allowing users to view prompts discreetly.\n*   **Input Methods:** Beyond real-time audio, the tool supports manual question entry and \"screenshot-to-answer\" functionality, where you can capture an image of a coding problem or question to receive an immediate AI-generated solution.\n*   **Control & Customization:** Users can manage the copilot through:\n    *   **Hotkeys & Shortcuts:** Customizable keyboard shortcuts allow you to interact with the tool (e.g., triggering answers or pausing the AI) without needing to click on the interface, helping maintain focus on the interview screen.\n    *   **Manual/Click-Through Modes:** These modes allow for finer control over when and how the AI provides information, ensuring it doesn't interrupt the natural flow of the conversation.\n*   **Live Human Backup:** Some versions of the service, often referred to as \"LockedIn Duo,\" offer an option to connect with live human backup for additional assistance during high-pressure scenarios.\n\n### Preparation & Usage\nBefore an interview, users typically configure the tool by uploading relevant documents (such as a resume or job description) and selecting presets that tailor the AI’s responses to the specific role or company. The platform also offers mock interview practice modes to help users get comfortable with the interface before their actual, high-stakes interviews.\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **Risk & Reliability:** While the tool is used to reduce nerves and provide quick answers, reviews often note that the output can sometimes sound generic or \"robotic.\" Relying on it blindly during a high-stakes interview is generally discouraged by experts, as the answers may not always follow a natural, conversational structure.\n*   **Policy Compliance:** Using AI assistants during interviews can violate the terms of service of certain platforms or the specific hiring policies of a company. Users are advised to be aware of the rules set by their prospective employers regarding the use of external tools."}
