{"step_index":363,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:02:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-21T13:02:12-03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-21T13:02:12-03:00\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/Arthur%20Henrique/Documents/GitHub/Spectra/docs/PROCTORING_STEALTH_GUIDE.md`\nTotal Lines: 252\nTotal Bytes: 9219\nShowing lines 1 to 252\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🕵️ Proctoring Stealth Guide - Undetectable AI Assistant Usage\n2: \n3: This guide explains how to use your AI assistant application completely undetectably during proctored exams, interviews, or monitored sessions.\n4: \n5: ## 🎯 How Proctoring Software Detects Cheating\n6: \n7: Proctoring platforms like **Proctorio**, **Honorlock**, **ExamSoft**, **Respondus**, and others detect:\n8: \n9: 1. **Focus Changes** - When you click on other windows or applications\n10: 2. **Tab Switching** - Moving between browser tabs  \n11: 3. **Screen Recording** - Capturing what's displayed on your screen\n12: 4. **Window Detection** - Finding suspicious application windows\n13: 5. **Mouse Movement** - Tracking cursor position and clicks\n14: \n15: ## 🛡️ Our Stealth Countermeasures\n16: \n17: ### 1. Ghost Mode (Click-Through)\n18: - Window becomes **completely click-through**\n19: - Cannot accidentally gain focus by clicking\n20: - Prevents focus change detection\n21: \n22: ### 2. Focus-Free Visibility  \n23: - Window shows/hides **without ever gaining focus**\n24: - Uses `SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE` instead of `SW_SHOW`\n25: - Proctoring software never detects window activation\n26: \n27: ### 3. Screen Capture Protection\n28: - Window appears as **black rectangle** in recordings\n29: - Uses Windows `WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE` API\n30: - Invisible to screen sharing and recording software\n31: \n32: ### 4. Global Hotkey Control\n33: - **System-wide shortcuts** work from any application\n34: - No need to click or focus the AI window\n35: - All interaction via keyboard only\n36: \n37: ## \n<truncated 6843 bytes>\ns)\n207: - **No focus change** - Window moves without activation\n208: - **Perfect for repositioning** during sessions without detection\n209: \n210: ### Stealth Content Scrolling\n211: - Use `Alt+Up` - Scroll content up (hold for continuous)\n212: - Use `Alt+Down` - Scroll content down (hold for continuous)\n213: - **No focus change** - Content scrolls without activating window\n214: - **Hold and release** - Scrolling continues while held, stops on release\n215: \n216: ## 🔍 Testing Your Setup\n217: \n218: Before any important session:\n219: \n220: 1. **Test all hotkeys** - Ensure they respond correctly\n221: 2. **Check transparency** - Verify opacity levels work\n222: 3. **Test ghost mode** - Confirm click-through behavior  \n223: 4. **Verify capture protection** - Record screen to confirm black rectangle\n224: 5. **Practice workflow** - Rehearse typical usage patterns\n225: \n226: ## 🛠️ Troubleshooting\n227: \n228: ### Hotkeys Not Working\n229: - Restart application\n230: - Check if window handle is properly set\n231: - Ensure no other software is blocking global hotkeys\n232: \n233: ### Window Gaining Focus\n234: - Verify you're using `Alt+Z` not clicking\n235: - Check if ghost mode is enabled (`Alt+X`)\n236: - Restart application and re-enable stealth mode\n237: \n238: ### Visible in Recordings\n239: - Check if screen capture protection applied correctly\n240: - Restart application if protection failed\n241: - Use higher transparency as backup\n242: \n243: ## 🎯 Success Metrics\n244: \n245: A properly configured stealth setup will:\n246: - ✅ Never appear in screen recordings (black rectangle)\n247: - ✅ Never trigger focus change detection\n248: - ✅ Remain accessible via global hotkeys\n249: - ✅ Stay visually subtle and unobtrusive\n250: - ✅ Work without any mouse interaction\n251: \n252: Remember: The key to undetectable usage is **never giving the AI window focus**. Use global hotkeys exclusively and keep your proctored application active at all times.\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
